1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:00,944
(All characters, locations,
and events are fictional

2
00:00:00,969 --> 00:00:01,920
and for entertainment
purposes only.

3
00:00:01,944 --> 00:00:02,887
No actions depicted are intended
to be encouraged or endorsed.

4
00:00:02,912 --> 00:00:03,960
Animals were specially trained
and supervised by professionals.

5
00:00:03,985 --> 00:00:05,404
Viewer discretion is advised.)

6
00:00:05,846 --> 00:00:07,972
In golf,
you can calculate everything.

7
00:00:07,997 --> 00:00:10,195
Distance, wind speed, and slope.

8
00:00:12,215 --> 00:00:14,216
But you can't calculate feelings.

9
00:00:16,522 --> 00:00:19,238
If you ask me what the most
stressful moment in golf is,

10
00:00:19,263 --> 00:00:22,011
for me, it's not when I'm
standing over the final putt.

11
00:00:22,036 --> 00:00:23,600
It's when I have to choose.

12
00:00:28,874 --> 00:00:31,471
Do I play it safe
or take the risk?

13
00:00:35,071 --> 00:00:38,663
Sometimes the best shot
isn't the safest one.

14
00:00:40,094 --> 00:00:41,310
Love is the same.

15
00:00:41,335 --> 00:00:44,216
Sometimes you have to take a risk
to reach the green.

16
00:00:47,837 --> 00:00:49,273
Because if you
never take the shot,

17
00:00:49,298 --> 00:00:51,868
you'll never know
how close you could've gotten.

18
00:00:53,909 --> 00:00:56,202
(Pro Pop:
Ploychompoo Wilairungrueng)

19
00:01:06,008 --> 00:01:09,533
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

20
00:01:10,171 --> 00:01:11,902
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

21
00:01:11,927 --> 00:01:15,333
♪ It's plain to see ♪

22
00:01:15,986 --> 00:01:17,837
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

23
00:01:17,862 --> 00:01:21,197
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

24
00:01:21,706 --> 00:01:23,516
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

25
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:27,099
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

26
00:01:27,467 --> 00:01:29,397
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

27
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:32,201
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

28
00:01:32,226 --> 00:01:34,226
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

29
00:01:34,251 --> 00:01:37,015
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

30
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:39,731
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

31
00:01:39,756 --> 00:01:43,727
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

32
00:01:43,752 --> 00:01:45,752
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

33
00:01:45,777 --> 00:01:48,456
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

34
00:01:48,481 --> 00:01:52,022
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

35
00:01:52,047 --> 00:01:56,836
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

36
00:01:56,861 --> 00:01:58,861
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

37
00:02:00,399 --> 00:02:02,069
We're going to a fashion show?

38
00:02:03,215 --> 00:02:04,905
Hello, Fahsai!

39
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:07,708
This is my team.
And this is Pro Vee.

40
00:02:07,870 --> 00:02:10,299
Fahsai! You didn't tell me
you were coming.

41
00:02:10,324 --> 00:02:12,967
We can talk about
that fashion show idea of yours.

42
00:02:12,992 --> 00:02:15,249
I don't really exercise at all.

43
00:02:15,274 --> 00:02:18,721
Give golf a try.
I promise you'll fall for it.

44
00:02:18,746 --> 00:02:20,295
You could start with
just nine holes.

45
00:02:20,382 --> 00:02:22,805
- Feeling possessive?
- Jealous.

46
00:02:25,113 --> 00:02:27,872
Am I allowed
to be jealous over you?

47
00:02:27,975 --> 00:02:29,626
Good question.

48
00:02:29,674 --> 00:02:32,528
If you do, you'd better
start staking your claim.

49
00:02:32,697 --> 00:02:34,713
Hello, my Nana.

50
00:02:35,891 --> 00:02:38,266
A clothing collection
for golfers.

51
00:02:38,291 --> 00:02:40,243
The collars need to be crisp.
Yes.

52
00:02:40,268 --> 00:02:42,300
And the fabric has to breathe.

53
00:02:42,325 --> 00:02:43,546
In hot weather,

54
00:02:43,570 --> 00:02:46,014
uncomfortable clothes will only
put people in a bad mood.

55
00:02:47,419 --> 00:02:49,347
Soft, but not soft enough.

56
00:02:49,372 --> 00:02:53,063
The texture needs to feel
effortlessly luxurious.

57
00:02:54,478 --> 00:02:58,809
Yes. Effortlessly luxurious.

58
00:03:04,202 --> 00:03:05,527
Sorry to interrupt, Nana.

59
00:03:06,535 --> 00:03:09,003
I wanted to update you
on our new memberships.

60
00:03:09,151 --> 00:03:13,206
New memberships are up
15 percent this month.

61
00:03:13,231 --> 00:03:16,020
Great. Another 15 percent softer
would be perfect.

62
00:03:16,694 --> 00:03:19,537
I meant the number of members.

63
00:03:20,172 --> 00:03:21,703
Oh! Right. That's great.

64
00:03:21,727 --> 00:03:24,636
Our membership
has really gone up.

65
00:03:24,874 --> 00:03:26,985
Okay. One more thing.

66
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:31,357
I wanted to ask you about
the new grass for the greens.

67
00:03:31,685 --> 00:03:33,665
We've got two options
from the supplier.

68
00:03:33,689 --> 00:03:37,316
The first has good green speed
but requires more maintenance.

69
00:03:37,341 --> 00:03:40,660
The other is more durable,
but the speed isn't as good.

70
00:03:40,685 --> 00:03:41,938
What do you think, Nana?

71
00:03:41,963 --> 00:03:44,247
If it needs too much care,
it won't work.

72
00:03:44,272 --> 00:03:47,078
We also have to consider washing,
ironing, and maintenance.

73
00:03:48,157 --> 00:03:52,296
Now I'm confused. What exactly
are you talking about?

74
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:56,054
- The texture.
- The texture of the grass?

75
00:03:57,410 --> 00:04:00,758
So we'll go with something
durable and low-maintenance.

76
00:04:00,783 --> 00:04:04,850
It should feel soft
and effortlessly luxurious.

77
00:04:05,310 --> 00:04:09,076
Wow. That's deep.

78
00:04:09,101 --> 00:04:12,413
I forgot about
how the green feels underfoot.

79
00:04:12,438 --> 00:04:15,757
Okay, then.
We'll go with that grass.

80
00:04:21,314 --> 00:04:24,386
This one's good too. It'll be
comfortable during a swing,

81
00:04:24,411 --> 00:04:26,411
and it'll look elegant in motion.

82
00:04:31,450 --> 00:04:33,174
Are you busy, Nana?

83
00:04:33,356 --> 00:04:35,047
Vee. What's up?

84
00:04:35,213 --> 00:04:39,680
Nut said you chose a durable
green with slower ball speed?

85
00:04:39,705 --> 00:04:42,772
- I haven't chosen anything yet.
- Then what's going on?

86
00:04:42,797 --> 00:04:45,298
This isn't soft enough.
We need the softer one.

87
00:04:45,323 --> 00:04:47,076
- The grass?
- The fabric.

88
00:04:47,906 --> 00:04:51,225
Weren't we talking about
the green and what grass to use?

89
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:54,037
Oh! Right. The grass.

90
00:04:54,221 --> 00:04:56,635
Vee, what do you think of
this fabric? Nice texture?

91
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:58,107
It'd make a beautiful green.

92
00:04:58,132 --> 00:04:59,766
- Nana.
- Yes?

93
00:04:59,790 --> 00:05:01,863
Which one of us is confused here?

94
00:05:01,888 --> 00:05:05,032
Sorry. Fabric and grass
are all mixed up in my head.

95
00:05:06,509 --> 00:05:08,143
Maybe focus on
one thing at a time.

96
00:05:08,168 --> 00:05:10,651
No one can focus on
two things at once.

97
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:13,678
Oh, Vee. Don't move.

98
00:05:15,888 --> 00:05:18,124
- Be my model.
- What?

99
00:05:18,149 --> 00:05:21,526
Remember the fashion show
I want to hold here?

100
00:05:21,551 --> 00:05:23,777
Besides professional models
and celebrities,

101
00:05:23,802 --> 00:05:26,483
I want our pros and staff
to walk the runway too.

102
00:05:28,594 --> 00:05:29,799
You think that's a good idea?

103
00:05:30,029 --> 00:05:31,394
Why wouldn't it be?

104
00:05:31,419 --> 00:05:34,595
You're gorgeous and cool,
and Nut's so handsome.

105
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:37,892
Everyone at our course
is ridiculously good-looking.

106
00:05:40,231 --> 00:05:42,896
Come on. Since you're here,
let me take your measurements.

107
00:06:04,842 --> 00:06:06,862
Isn't the measuring tape enough?

108
00:06:06,887 --> 00:06:10,116
You don't need to measure me with
your eyes too. You're staring.

109
00:06:10,522 --> 00:06:14,720
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

110
00:06:15,504 --> 00:06:20,123
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

111
00:06:20,641 --> 00:06:25,185
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

112
00:06:25,751 --> 00:06:29,144
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

113
00:06:29,169 --> 00:06:30,213
Are you done yet?

114
00:06:31,561 --> 00:06:35,270
Not yet.
I still need to measure... here.

115
00:06:37,545 --> 00:06:42,277
I wonder if someone's
already in your heart.

116
00:06:42,302 --> 00:06:45,465
Are all four chambers
already taken?

117
00:06:45,490 --> 00:06:49,062
I wonder if there's any room
for your Nana.

118
00:06:49,975 --> 00:06:55,822
What if I gave you all four?
Could you take care of them?

119
00:06:55,858 --> 00:06:59,152
Of course. As long as
I'm the only one in there.

120
00:07:01,521 --> 00:07:04,632
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

121
00:07:04,657 --> 00:07:07,269
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

122
00:07:07,726 --> 00:07:10,226
Stealing a drop
without permission?

123
00:07:10,251 --> 00:07:12,733
That's a penalty
under the rules of golf.

124
00:07:13,188 --> 00:07:16,282
Hmm...
What should the penalty be?

125
00:07:16,482 --> 00:07:18,982
Now you have to even things out.

126
00:07:26,758 --> 00:07:31,234
Clever and sneaky as ever,
Miss Nana.

127
00:07:34,722 --> 00:07:39,440
♪ One look in your eyes
is all I need ♪

128
00:07:39,465 --> 00:07:43,062
♪ Oh, baby. I trust your sweet. ♪

129
00:07:49,521 --> 00:07:51,076
What can I do for you,
Ms. Yupadee?

130
00:07:52,464 --> 00:07:54,420
Have you seen the news
about Goodview's event?

131
00:07:55,246 --> 00:07:58,393
You mean the fashion show?

132
00:08:00,189 --> 00:08:02,531
- I have.
- What do you think?

133
00:08:03,082 --> 00:08:06,234
They must be running out of ideas
to compete with us.

134
00:08:06,695 --> 00:08:08,996
That's why they're resorting to
something so ridiculous.

135
00:08:09,166 --> 00:08:13,516
It's a golf course.
It's right there in the name.

136
00:08:14,906 --> 00:08:17,023
Nana must've lost her mind.

137
00:08:18,081 --> 00:08:21,033
You really think so?

138
00:08:22,532 --> 00:08:23,810
From what I've seen,

139
00:08:23,834 --> 00:08:26,690
Goodview's event is getting
a lot of attention.

140
00:08:27,471 --> 00:08:28,907
And the feedback is good.

141
00:08:29,451 --> 00:08:31,522
People are probably interested
because it's unusual.

142
00:08:32,579 --> 00:08:35,972
It's a publicity stunt
to get people talking.

143
00:08:36,496 --> 00:08:38,869
The buzz will die down
soon enough.

144
00:08:39,309 --> 00:08:40,708
It won't last.

145
00:08:43,002 --> 00:08:44,304
And what about my course?

146
00:08:45,929 --> 00:08:49,896
You said you had new ideas,
but I haven't seen a single one.

147
00:08:50,009 --> 00:08:53,360
All you've done
is poach Goodview's former staff.

148
00:08:56,354 --> 00:08:57,978
Take it easy, Ms. Yupadee.

149
00:08:58,939 --> 00:09:00,788
It's not that
I don't have a plan.

150
00:09:01,838 --> 00:09:04,398
I'm just waiting
for the right moment.

151
00:09:06,568 --> 00:09:07,774
With something like this,

152
00:09:08,850 --> 00:09:10,706
if we're gonna play,
we play hard.

153
00:09:12,725 --> 00:09:16,199
Hard enough
to leave them speechless.

154
00:09:27,712 --> 00:09:30,569
Everyone's outfits
have been updated and are ready.

155
00:09:30,594 --> 00:09:32,594
After practice,
let's go try them on.

156
00:09:32,619 --> 00:09:37,256
Sure. But I want to walk the
runway too. I've been practicing.

157
00:09:37,289 --> 00:09:39,880
They say models need
a proper model face.

158
00:09:39,905 --> 00:09:43,805
Smile, raise the brows,
relax the lips... and walk.

159
00:09:44,217 --> 00:09:46,256
Absolutely.
I'll make you an outfit too.

160
00:09:46,281 --> 00:09:47,533
Okay!

161
00:09:47,683 --> 00:09:51,389
Actually, no. I need to
handle the food and drinks.

162
00:09:51,414 --> 00:09:53,934
If I'm not there,
what's everyone going to eat?

163
00:09:53,959 --> 00:09:56,195
Besides, I'd totally
outshine all the models.

164
00:09:57,712 --> 00:10:03,425
Belle, are the models' and
celebrities' outfits all set?

165
00:10:03,450 --> 00:10:07,241
Everything's on track. Fahsai is
coming this afternoon to help.

166
00:10:07,851 --> 00:10:10,562
Fahsai?
She's coming this afternoon?

167
00:10:10,689 --> 00:10:13,503
- Yes.
- Hmm. That's too bad.

168
00:10:13,528 --> 00:10:18,088
Pro Vee and I have to go
check out the golf gear

169
00:10:18,113 --> 00:10:20,519
our sponsors are providing
for the event.

170
00:10:25,274 --> 00:10:29,118
Unless you'd rather stay
and help Fahsai?

171
00:10:29,143 --> 00:10:30,888
I can go alone.

172
00:10:33,027 --> 00:10:34,774
Whatever you say, Miss Nana.

173
00:10:38,878 --> 00:10:42,448
All right, everyone.
Ready for our first rehearsal?

174
00:10:42,473 --> 00:10:44,164
- Ready!
- Ready!

175
00:10:44,252 --> 00:10:46,797
Hmm? What's with that energy?

176
00:10:46,822 --> 00:10:48,487
I know you can do this.

177
00:10:48,512 --> 00:10:50,126
Have a little confidence
in yourselves.

178
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:52,356
Come on! Let's hear some energy.
Ready?

179
00:10:52,570 --> 00:10:54,237
- Ready!
- Ready!

180
00:10:59,673 --> 00:11:03,080
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

181
00:11:03,818 --> 00:11:05,669
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

182
00:11:05,694 --> 00:11:09,189
♪ It's plain to see ♪

183
00:11:09,571 --> 00:11:11,468
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

184
00:11:11,493 --> 00:11:14,662
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

185
00:11:15,386 --> 00:11:17,259
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

186
00:11:17,284 --> 00:11:20,611
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

187
00:11:21,052 --> 00:11:23,052
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

188
00:11:23,077 --> 00:11:25,849
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

189
00:11:25,874 --> 00:11:28,034
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

190
00:11:28,059 --> 00:11:30,513
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

191
00:11:30,538 --> 00:11:33,516
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

192
00:11:33,541 --> 00:11:37,225
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

193
00:11:37,250 --> 00:11:39,250
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

194
00:11:41,258 --> 00:11:43,258
So handsome!

195
00:11:45,714 --> 00:11:49,812
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

196
00:11:50,663 --> 00:11:53,244
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

197
00:11:53,269 --> 00:11:56,596
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

198
00:11:56,621 --> 00:12:00,310
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

199
00:12:00,335 --> 00:12:03,097
Gorgeous!

200
00:12:06,419 --> 00:12:07,729
Beautiful.

201
00:12:16,416 --> 00:12:17,939
Let's put on a face mask

202
00:12:17,964 --> 00:12:19,566
so you'll look gorgeous
on the big day.

203
00:12:19,654 --> 00:12:21,812
No. I don't like them.
They're all sticky.

204
00:12:34,982 --> 00:12:37,905
This one's not sticky.
Don't be difficult.

205
00:12:37,930 --> 00:12:40,508
I don't want you to be
the odd one out on the catwalk.

206
00:12:41,134 --> 00:12:43,624
Do I look that bad to you?

207
00:12:45,070 --> 00:12:47,820
To me, you're beautiful.

208
00:12:47,845 --> 00:12:51,720
But I want everyone else to
notice how beautiful you are too.

209
00:12:53,527 --> 00:12:55,439
Aren't you afraid
someone might hit on me?

210
00:12:56,757 --> 00:12:59,465
I hope they do. Then I'll know
you're really beautiful,

211
00:12:59,490 --> 00:13:00,961
and it's not just me
who thinks so.

212
00:13:01,381 --> 00:13:03,762
If someone really does hit on me,

213
00:13:04,361 --> 00:13:05,919
don't regret it later.

214
00:13:06,792 --> 00:13:11,087
You had first dibs
and didn't make your move.

215
00:13:12,551 --> 00:13:14,233
I don't make the first move.

216
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:18,142
When it's the right person,
one look is enough.

217
00:13:18,564 --> 00:13:22,861
No need for words.
No need to waste time flirting.

218
00:13:29,724 --> 00:13:31,109
Do you know now?

219
00:13:32,962 --> 00:13:37,511
No. You still look
a little unsure, Pro Jin.

220
00:13:44,236 --> 00:13:47,950
How about now?
Is that clear enough?

221
00:13:53,492 --> 00:13:54,539
Now do you know?

222
00:14:22,064 --> 00:14:23,877
Your skin is so smooth.

223
00:14:27,248 --> 00:14:31,570
And this nose...
under the catwalk lights,

224
00:14:32,205 --> 00:14:33,879
it'll stand out even more.

225
00:14:36,798 --> 00:14:42,269
When you're blessed with beauty,
you've got to take care of it.

226
00:14:56,146 --> 00:14:57,178
All done.

227
00:14:57,853 --> 00:14:59,154
Here. Let me do yours.

228
00:14:59,543 --> 00:15:02,466
It's okay.
I prefer doing it myself.

229
00:15:03,330 --> 00:15:06,477
All right. Leave it on for
20 minutes, then rinse it off.

230
00:15:54,798 --> 00:15:57,559
I saw your light was still on,
so I figured you were awake.

231
00:15:58,695 --> 00:15:59,735
Here.

232
00:16:02,486 --> 00:16:03,913
Thanks.

233
00:16:04,128 --> 00:16:07,191
I just want to make absolutely
sure nothing goes wrong tomorrow.

234
00:16:09,450 --> 00:16:12,859
You can't keep losing sleep.
You'll wear yourself out.

235
00:16:13,473 --> 00:16:16,499
I'm fine. I just want to
check one more thing.

236
00:16:16,524 --> 00:16:18,382
You've checked it
at least ten times.

237
00:16:18,407 --> 00:16:20,129
Don't you have to
get up early tomorrow?

238
00:16:20,153 --> 00:16:23,210
- Very early.
- Then go to bed.

239
00:16:24,023 --> 00:16:26,982
I won't be able to sleep.
I'm too excited.

240
00:16:27,007 --> 00:16:29,607
I can't wait to see how
everything turns out tomorrow.

241
00:16:30,188 --> 00:16:34,676
It'll be great. You've personally
overseen every detail.

242
00:16:35,161 --> 00:16:38,744
But honestly,
I'm a little nervous too.

243
00:16:38,990 --> 00:16:41,262
I'm worried
I'll miss this or forget that.

244
00:16:41,287 --> 00:16:43,583
Hmm... come here.

245
00:16:57,651 --> 00:16:59,976
Vee... is this really okay?

246
00:17:00,001 --> 00:17:02,702
I'm not ready yet.
And tomorrow...

247
00:17:02,727 --> 00:17:04,487
What do you think
I'm going to do?

248
00:17:05,033 --> 00:17:06,042
Well...

249
00:17:07,519 --> 00:17:10,830
- Well...
- Well, what?

250
00:17:12,130 --> 00:17:17,179
I mean a moment like this,
just the two of us...

251
00:17:24,427 --> 00:17:25,983
Vee...

252
00:17:31,132 --> 00:17:33,117
- Go to sleep.
- Hmm?

253
00:17:33,268 --> 00:17:35,724
- I brought you here to sleep.
- Oh?

254
00:17:43,844 --> 00:17:45,718
Come here.
I'll massage your hands.

255
00:17:53,251 --> 00:17:54,626
That feels so good.

256
00:17:57,008 --> 00:18:00,241
When I was little, I'd practice
every day before a tournament.

257
00:18:00,266 --> 00:18:02,935
Mom would do this
whenever I couldn't sleep.

258
00:18:03,439 --> 00:18:04,453
Feel better?

259
00:18:06,088 --> 00:18:07,090
Much better.

260
00:18:25,532 --> 00:18:26,590
Nana?

261
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:31,347
That was fast.

262
00:18:41,239 --> 00:18:42,284
Sweet dreams.

263
00:18:58,884 --> 00:19:00,926
Jeab, put the flowers
right here, please.

264
00:19:03,150 --> 00:19:04,484
And this one over here.

265
00:19:09,570 --> 00:19:10,726
Thank you so much.

266
00:19:17,811 --> 00:19:21,086
- How's everything going?
- Everything's ready.

267
00:19:27,136 --> 00:19:30,770
Pro Vee, let me check
everything for you.

268
00:19:32,678 --> 00:19:35,301
Does this fit okay?
You look gorgeous.

269
00:19:35,326 --> 00:19:37,579
Nana, could you come over here?

270
00:19:40,203 --> 00:19:43,910
Could you give me
one final check? Just to be safe.

271
00:19:48,489 --> 00:19:53,825
Fahsai, could you go double-check
that area... over there?

272
00:19:55,171 --> 00:19:57,568
Way over there.
Could you do that for me?

273
00:19:58,193 --> 00:20:00,793
- Me?
- Mm-hmm. Please?

274
00:20:01,495 --> 00:20:03,763
- Love you.
- That's so far!

275
00:20:08,542 --> 00:20:10,567
Everything looks fine, Vee.

276
00:20:10,925 --> 00:20:14,767
Maybe I just needed a little
encouragement. I'm nervous.

277
00:20:15,378 --> 00:20:18,232
What are you nervous about?
This is our golf course.

278
00:20:18,257 --> 00:20:20,771
You know every inch of it
better than anyone.

279
00:20:21,086 --> 00:20:22,674
You've got this.

280
00:20:24,550 --> 00:20:28,002
Everyone, fifteen minutes!
Are we ready?

281
00:20:28,541 --> 00:20:30,220
- No!
- Not ready!

282
00:20:31,533 --> 00:20:33,134
Well, I'm ready!

283
00:20:33,159 --> 00:20:36,432
I had my Douyin makeup done
extra glamorous.

284
00:20:39,747 --> 00:20:43,193
- I'm nervous, Nana.
- What is everyone so scared of?

285
00:20:44,134 --> 00:20:47,914
Come on. Let's put our hands in
and get some energy going.

286
00:20:47,939 --> 00:20:50,527
- Come on, gather around...
- So this is where everyone is.

287
00:20:50,552 --> 00:20:53,529
- Sir!
- Dad? What are you doing here?

288
00:20:53,554 --> 00:20:56,612
Our VVIP belongs in
the front row over there!

289
00:20:56,637 --> 00:20:58,919
Eh? I came to cheer you on.

290
00:20:58,944 --> 00:21:02,644
Aww, that's so sweet.
Come give us a boost too, Dad.

291
00:21:02,669 --> 00:21:04,669
A boost? How?

292
00:21:05,854 --> 00:21:08,774
All right, everyone. Vive la vie!

293
00:21:08,799 --> 00:21:09,952
Vive la what-the-what?

294
00:21:09,976 --> 00:21:12,421
Yes! One more time.
One, two, three!

295
00:21:12,446 --> 00:21:15,249
- Vive la vie!
- Vive la vie!

296
00:21:17,171 --> 00:21:22,523
Oh, I feel it now!
That's a boost!

297
00:21:22,548 --> 00:21:24,803
- Looking handsome today.
- Thank you, Miss.

298
00:21:49,019 --> 00:21:51,964
♪ Say it, say it.
Say "You love me." ♪

299
00:21:51,989 --> 00:21:54,930
♪ Call me, call me.
Call me "Baby." ♪

300
00:22:01,040 --> 00:22:03,716
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

301
00:22:03,741 --> 00:22:06,559
♪ Just one more little try,
my dear ♪

302
00:22:06,584 --> 00:22:09,434
♪ Or we'll be wasting
one whole year ♪

303
00:22:09,459 --> 00:22:11,459
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

304
00:22:11,484 --> 00:22:14,327
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

305
00:22:14,352 --> 00:22:17,218
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

306
00:22:17,243 --> 00:22:21,023
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

307
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:23,048
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

308
00:22:23,073 --> 00:22:25,815
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

309
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:29,397
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

310
00:22:29,422 --> 00:22:33,786
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

311
00:22:33,811 --> 00:22:35,811
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

312
00:22:35,836 --> 00:22:38,471
♪ Say it, say it.
Say "You love me." ♪

313
00:22:38,496 --> 00:22:41,426
♪ Call me, call me.
Call me "Baby." ♪

314
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:49,187
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

315
00:22:49,212 --> 00:22:52,691
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

316
00:22:52,716 --> 00:22:57,409
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

317
00:22:57,434 --> 00:22:59,434
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

318
00:23:01,691 --> 00:23:05,157
That was amazing!
Thank you so much, everyone.

319
00:23:05,990 --> 00:23:07,263
You did great, sweetheart.

320
00:23:15,288 --> 00:23:19,108
- You did so well.
- Amazing.

321
00:23:22,031 --> 00:23:24,037
Thank you all so much.

322
00:23:24,062 --> 00:23:27,068
This wouldn't have turned out
half as well without all of you.

323
00:23:27,093 --> 00:23:30,128
It turned out even better
than I imagined.

324
00:23:30,473 --> 00:23:32,768
We had over ten thousand viewers
on the livestream.

325
00:23:32,793 --> 00:23:34,484
Our highest ever.

326
00:23:35,905 --> 00:23:39,073
Online is one thing,
but seeing everyone in person...

327
00:23:39,098 --> 00:23:43,411
You're all gorgeous.
I'm seriously impressed.

328
00:23:46,171 --> 00:23:48,362
At first,
all I could think about was

329
00:23:48,387 --> 00:23:51,387
how to bring this course
back to life.

330
00:23:51,412 --> 00:23:55,363
But today I realized we don't
just have a beautiful course.

331
00:23:55,388 --> 00:23:57,316
We also have talented,

332
00:23:57,341 --> 00:23:59,669
forward-thinking people
ready to move forward together.

333
00:23:59,694 --> 00:24:02,945
That's because you made us
believe in ourselves, Miss Nana.

334
00:24:02,970 --> 00:24:05,740
- Right, everyone?
- Absolutely!

335
00:24:05,978 --> 00:24:07,434
Thank you. I really mean it.

336
00:24:07,459 --> 00:24:12,228
And we've still got a lot
more fun things ahead of us.

337
00:24:12,253 --> 00:24:13,660
So let's keep going together.

338
00:24:15,207 --> 00:24:19,466
Vive la vie! Vive la vie!

339
00:24:19,491 --> 00:24:26,600
Allez! Allez!

340
00:24:26,625 --> 00:24:33,378
Allez! Allez!

341
00:24:33,402 --> 00:24:36,597
Allez! Allez!

342
00:24:36,622 --> 00:24:39,147
Nana, are you okay?

343
00:24:40,266 --> 00:24:43,402
I'm fine.

344
00:24:46,155 --> 00:24:48,362
- Hey!
- Miss Nana!

345
00:24:48,387 --> 00:24:50,477
- Nana!
- Call an ambulance!

346
00:24:50,502 --> 00:24:54,079
- Anyone have smelling salts?
- Any smelling salts?

347
00:24:54,104 --> 00:24:56,503
Don't crowd her.
Give her some space.

348
00:25:07,122 --> 00:25:09,659
Hey, she's awake!

349
00:25:18,467 --> 00:25:22,735
I'm in the hospital, right?
What happened?

350
00:25:23,430 --> 00:25:25,893
You were talking to me,
then suddenly you just fainted.

351
00:25:26,242 --> 00:25:27,560
You scared all of us.

352
00:25:28,253 --> 00:25:31,041
Seriously.
You know what I thought?

353
00:25:31,066 --> 00:25:33,741
I thought this was like
one of those dramas

354
00:25:33,766 --> 00:25:35,344
where someone suddenly collapses

355
00:25:35,368 --> 00:25:39,004
because they've been secretly
hiding some terrible illness

356
00:25:39,029 --> 00:25:40,312
and never told anyone.

357
00:25:40,439 --> 00:25:41,931
Enough with the drama, Queen.

358
00:25:41,956 --> 00:25:44,565
The doctor said Nana just
hasn't been resting enough.

359
00:25:44,590 --> 00:25:46,112
She's just exhausted.

360
00:25:48,297 --> 00:25:50,705
You can't keep
pushing yourself this hard.

361
00:25:50,730 --> 00:25:52,937
You need to
take care of yourself too.

362
00:25:53,507 --> 00:25:57,188
Just remember, you have me
here to handle things,

363
00:25:57,213 --> 00:26:01,489
and everyone at Goodview
is always here to support you.

364
00:26:07,303 --> 00:26:10,455
Hello? What game
are you talking about?

365
00:26:10,844 --> 00:26:13,352
I'm at the hospital.
I'm not playing tonight.

366
00:26:18,134 --> 00:26:20,216
My friends want me to play.
One sec.

367
00:26:25,972 --> 00:26:27,876
No, I'm not playing.
I'm at the hospital.

368
00:26:32,054 --> 00:26:34,177
- Oh, Mr. Sanchai.
- Doctor. Hello.

369
00:26:34,202 --> 00:26:36,018
Hello.
What brings you here today?

370
00:26:36,043 --> 00:26:39,268
My daughter overworked herself
and fainted,

371
00:26:39,293 --> 00:26:41,268
so she's staying here
for a couple of days.

372
00:26:41,293 --> 00:26:45,630
I see. And what about
your chemotherapy plan?

373
00:26:46,362 --> 00:26:48,713
Have you decided
when you'd like to start?

374
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:56,737
I haven't really decided yet.

375
00:26:57,158 --> 00:26:59,158
I'll get back to you
as soon as I can.

376
00:27:00,690 --> 00:27:02,745
All right.
But don't wait too long.

377
00:27:02,770 --> 00:27:04,404
It could spread further.

378
00:27:06,049 --> 00:27:08,269
- Understood. Thank you, Doctor.
- Excuse me, then.

379
00:27:18,091 --> 00:27:21,683
Chemo? Dad has cancer?

380
00:27:29,571 --> 00:27:32,447
Her vitals are normal.
No fever or other symptoms.

381
00:27:32,472 --> 00:27:35,501
She may just be experiencing
fatigue, as the doctor mentioned.

382
00:27:35,526 --> 00:27:37,526
Okay. Thank you very much.

383
00:27:44,754 --> 00:27:45,825
You're okay now, dear.

384
00:27:46,667 --> 00:27:48,411
Since you're already
in the hospital,

385
00:27:48,435 --> 00:27:51,564
why don't you get
a full checkup while you're here?

386
00:27:55,682 --> 00:27:58,254
He's right, Miss Nana.
Your health is important.

387
00:27:58,279 --> 00:28:02,105
I may look like a little pig,
but I'm a very healthy pig.

388
00:28:03,339 --> 00:28:05,324
I'm really fine.

389
00:28:05,686 --> 00:28:07,598
Get checked anyway.

390
00:28:07,623 --> 00:28:09,979
You've still got plenty of
projects ahead of you.

391
00:28:14,613 --> 00:28:15,686
All right.

392
00:28:16,227 --> 00:28:19,116
Good. Now get some rest.

393
00:28:20,273 --> 00:28:23,168
If there's nothing else,
we should all head home

394
00:28:23,193 --> 00:28:24,645
so Nana can get some proper rest.

395
00:28:24,670 --> 00:28:26,497
Oh, wait, sir...

396
00:28:26,734 --> 00:28:30,156
Isn't anyone
staying overnight with her?

397
00:28:30,181 --> 00:28:32,967
It's okay. Everyone must be
exhausted already.

398
00:28:32,992 --> 00:28:39,195
Oh, no, Miss Nana!
Hospitals have ghosts, you know.

399
00:28:39,220 --> 00:28:41,045
Haven't you heard
all those scary stories

400
00:28:41,070 --> 00:28:43,103
about ghosts under hospital beds?

401
00:28:43,128 --> 00:28:45,045
You'll never get any sleep.

402
00:28:46,714 --> 00:28:49,953
Then can you
stay with Nana, Chef Queen?

403
00:28:50,360 --> 00:28:51,678
- Chef Queen... Me?
- Yes.

404
00:28:52,538 --> 00:28:57,127
I mean, I could...
but around two in the morning,

405
00:28:57,152 --> 00:28:59,740
I tend to wake up
and snore like this.

406
00:28:59,765 --> 00:29:02,891
Yes, exactly like this.

407
00:29:03,066 --> 00:29:07,073
You wouldn't get any rest at all.
So I'm definitely not suitable.

408
00:29:07,098 --> 00:29:09,782
Then I'll stay with Miss Nana.

409
00:29:10,757 --> 00:29:13,687
Belle, you have
a mountain of paperwork waiting.

410
00:29:13,712 --> 00:29:15,722
With Miss Nana away,

411
00:29:15,747 --> 00:29:17,992
you really should stay
and take care of all that.

412
00:29:19,058 --> 00:29:21,272
Oh... right. That's true.

413
00:29:22,826 --> 00:29:24,190
Right, Miss Nana?

414
00:29:25,627 --> 00:29:28,040
Uh... yes.

415
00:29:28,470 --> 00:29:30,214
See? Belle really
isn't the right person.

416
00:29:30,239 --> 00:29:31,255
Go get some work done.

417
00:29:32,660 --> 00:29:35,050
Gus, can you stay
with your sister tonight?

418
00:29:35,075 --> 00:29:38,871
Gus! Don't you have work
at the course?

419
00:29:39,648 --> 00:29:42,017
And besides, a man and a woman,
sharing a bathroom?

420
00:29:42,042 --> 00:29:44,812
That'd be awkward.

421
00:29:44,837 --> 00:29:46,338
Oh, just go home!

422
00:29:46,363 --> 00:29:48,554
Then I'll hire a private nurse
to stay with Nana.

423
00:29:48,579 --> 00:29:51,987
Oh, no, Sir. You can't just use
any nurse on duty.

424
00:29:52,012 --> 00:29:54,245
What's going on?
No one I suggest is good enough.

425
00:29:54,270 --> 00:29:56,372
Then I'll stay with Nana tonight.

426
00:29:56,397 --> 00:29:58,270
Oh! Now that makes sense.

427
00:29:58,517 --> 00:30:01,992
See? She's the perfect choice.

428
00:30:07,771 --> 00:30:11,020
Perfect! Pro Vee,
you're free tonight, right?

429
00:30:11,045 --> 00:30:12,064
I am.

430
00:30:13,129 --> 00:30:15,910
Don't worry, Sir.
They can take care of each other.

431
00:30:15,935 --> 00:30:20,216
Now, why don't we all head home?

432
00:30:21,503 --> 00:30:22,753
After you, Sir.

433
00:30:23,721 --> 00:30:27,049
I'll have the club driver
bring some clothes over for you.

434
00:30:27,074 --> 00:30:28,096
Thank you.

435
00:30:32,363 --> 00:30:34,011
Get some rest, dear, okay?

436
00:30:35,789 --> 00:30:37,051
Thank you, Pro Vee.

437
00:30:38,463 --> 00:30:41,739
We should get going, Sir.
After you.

438
00:30:41,764 --> 00:30:42,947
Let's go.

439
00:30:48,089 --> 00:30:49,289
After you, Sir.

440
00:30:54,123 --> 00:30:55,618
This way, please.

441
00:31:06,248 --> 00:31:07,436
Thank you.

442
00:31:14,840 --> 00:31:18,435
- I'll be heading off, then.
- I'll go with you.

443
00:31:20,226 --> 00:31:23,394
I'll get going too, Sir.
Good night.

444
00:31:23,419 --> 00:31:25,085
- Get home safely.
- I will.

445
00:31:26,713 --> 00:31:28,338
- Dad.
- What is it?

446
00:31:29,299 --> 00:31:31,703
You really should get
a health checkup sometime.

447
00:31:32,743 --> 00:31:33,780
Why?

448
00:31:35,463 --> 00:31:38,042
I'm perfectly healthy.
Why would I need a checkup?

449
00:31:40,354 --> 00:31:41,479
Are you sure, Dad?

450
00:31:42,409 --> 00:31:44,386
Do I look unhealthy to you?

451
00:31:44,411 --> 00:31:46,872
I play golf every single day.

452
00:31:46,897 --> 00:31:50,732
I can still drive the ball
300 yards.

453
00:31:50,830 --> 00:31:52,791
How could I possibly look sick?

454
00:31:52,816 --> 00:31:55,068
What about you?
Don't you have class tomorrow?

455
00:31:58,158 --> 00:31:59,400
Come on. Let's go home.

456
00:32:37,255 --> 00:32:38,452
Where are you going?

457
00:32:40,549 --> 00:32:42,098
To the bathroom.

458
00:32:42,217 --> 00:32:43,439
I'll take you.

459
00:32:43,464 --> 00:32:45,907
It's okay. I can go by myself.

460
00:32:46,437 --> 00:32:49,794
What if you faint again?
Let me help you.

461
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:57,216
Don't lock the bathroom door.

462
00:32:58,107 --> 00:32:59,160
Why not?

463
00:32:59,184 --> 00:33:02,506
In case you faint or fall,
so I can get to you right away.

464
00:33:06,599 --> 00:33:11,182
Vee, you don't have to stand
that close to the door.

465
00:33:11,767 --> 00:33:13,139
I'm not going to peek.

466
00:33:13,385 --> 00:33:16,473
It's not about peeking.
It's about...

467
00:33:17,828 --> 00:33:18,875
the sound.

468
00:33:20,225 --> 00:33:23,996
Then I'll turn the music up
so you won't feel embarrassed.

469
00:33:45,191 --> 00:33:47,545
All done?
Come on, I'll help you.

470
00:34:08,257 --> 00:34:09,347
Go to sleep.

471
00:34:15,868 --> 00:34:17,510
Will you massage my hands?

472
00:34:18,637 --> 00:34:19,653
Hmm?

473
00:34:20,637 --> 00:34:21,900
Like you did last night.

474
00:34:30,373 --> 00:34:31,373
Come here.

475
00:34:33,958 --> 00:34:38,418
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

476
00:34:39,107 --> 00:34:44,141
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

477
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:48,693
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

478
00:34:49,403 --> 00:34:53,745
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

479
00:34:54,432 --> 00:34:59,609
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

480
00:34:59,634 --> 00:35:03,939
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

481
00:35:04,601 --> 00:35:07,833
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

482
00:35:07,858 --> 00:35:10,313
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

483
00:35:10,338 --> 00:35:15,855
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

484
00:35:15,880 --> 00:35:18,956
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

485
00:35:18,981 --> 00:35:23,348
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

486
00:35:23,607 --> 00:35:25,024
Let me wipe your mouth.

487
00:35:25,484 --> 00:35:27,484
Miss Nana, about the fashion...

488
00:35:31,183 --> 00:35:32,501
Come in, Belle.

489
00:35:33,375 --> 00:35:36,303
I feel like
I came at a bad time.

490
00:35:37,773 --> 00:35:39,008
Want some water?

491
00:35:42,139 --> 00:35:43,163
Thank you.

492
00:35:47,867 --> 00:35:50,946
- Go ahead.
- What about the fashion show?

493
00:35:51,456 --> 00:35:55,349
I had a wrap-up meeting
with the event team yesterday,

494
00:35:55,374 --> 00:35:57,883
and the response
has been amazing.

495
00:35:58,139 --> 00:36:00,657
Four or five clients
called this morning

496
00:36:00,682 --> 00:36:03,406
asking about renting our course
for their own events.

497
00:36:03,674 --> 00:36:06,869
And both of our pros have
started getting job offers too.

498
00:36:06,894 --> 00:36:10,986
People have been calling to ask
their rates for product reviews.

499
00:36:11,910 --> 00:36:13,315
You did it.

500
00:36:13,438 --> 00:36:17,222
Our course is becoming more than
just a place to play golf.

501
00:36:17,346 --> 00:36:19,744
Oh, and I don't know
if it's a coincidence,

502
00:36:19,769 --> 00:36:21,642
but four of your students

503
00:36:21,667 --> 00:36:24,136
have already renewed
their lesson packages.

504
00:36:24,161 --> 00:36:26,462
And people have been asking

505
00:36:26,487 --> 00:36:28,720
about the collection
from yesterday's show too.

506
00:36:28,745 --> 00:36:30,467
They want to know
where they can buy it.

507
00:36:31,650 --> 00:36:34,710
Then why don't we start taking
orders through our pro shop?

508
00:36:40,134 --> 00:36:41,593
- Hello.
- Hello.

509
00:36:42,022 --> 00:36:44,664
- How are you feeling?
- Back to normal.

510
00:36:44,689 --> 00:36:46,498
Can I leave the hospital yet?

511
00:36:46,523 --> 00:36:48,523
I really want to
get back to work.

512
00:36:48,815 --> 00:36:50,672
Overall, you look fine.

513
00:36:50,969 --> 00:36:53,366
But let's wait
for your checkup results first.

514
00:36:53,517 --> 00:36:56,549
If everything looks good,
you can go home this afternoon.

515
00:36:57,057 --> 00:36:59,354
- Okay.
- Thank you.

516
00:36:59,386 --> 00:37:00,396
Thank you, Doctor.

517
00:37:03,412 --> 00:37:06,274
Belle, can you look after
Nana for me?

518
00:37:06,299 --> 00:37:09,747
I have lessons this afternoon,
but I'll come back this evening.

519
00:37:09,940 --> 00:37:11,560
Of course. Don't worry.

520
00:37:12,662 --> 00:37:13,940
I'll be back.

521
00:37:21,487 --> 00:37:24,882
Look at this. Goodview's
fashion show yesterday.

522
00:37:25,495 --> 00:37:27,201
People were checking in nonstop.

523
00:37:28,734 --> 00:37:30,686
It's probably
just a passing trend.

524
00:37:30,711 --> 00:37:31,741
It'll die down soon.

525
00:37:32,130 --> 00:37:34,622
Then start putting
that plan of yours into action.

526
00:37:35,142 --> 00:37:37,166
Stop talking and prove yourself.

527
00:37:37,191 --> 00:37:40,682
Don't make me think
it's no coincidence

528
00:37:40,877 --> 00:37:44,140
that Goodview has only
gotten better since you left.

529
00:37:44,286 --> 00:37:45,302
Ms. Yupadee.

530
00:37:47,448 --> 00:37:48,776
Isn't that a little harsh?

531
00:37:49,537 --> 00:37:50,965
I can be much harsher.

532
00:37:51,992 --> 00:37:57,623
Especially if I start thinking
I made a mistake hiring you.

533
00:37:59,982 --> 00:38:01,709
You won't regret hiring me.

534
00:38:04,234 --> 00:38:07,327
Then show me
this plan you keep talking about.

535
00:38:10,868 --> 00:38:11,876
Yes.

536
00:38:13,066 --> 00:38:15,474
You'll be wanting
to give me a raise soon enough.

537
00:38:30,724 --> 00:38:32,082
Vee, are you taking me...

538
00:38:32,545 --> 00:38:35,457
- Hi!
- Home...

539
00:38:36,376 --> 00:38:37,970
Oh. Fahsai.

540
00:38:37,995 --> 00:38:40,352
How are you?
I ran into Pro Vee at the course,

541
00:38:40,377 --> 00:38:42,407
so I tagged along to see you.

542
00:38:42,615 --> 00:38:45,216
I'm fine. The doctor said I just
haven't been resting enough.

543
00:38:45,534 --> 00:38:48,474
That's what I thought.
You're usually so healthy.

544
00:38:48,499 --> 00:38:55,007
I brought you some shrimp congee.
This place is amazing.

545
00:38:57,003 --> 00:39:01,070
- Thanks.
- But Nana's allergic to shrimp.

546
00:39:04,594 --> 00:39:08,362
Really? I had no idea.

547
00:39:11,463 --> 00:39:12,868
You remembered.

548
00:39:17,471 --> 00:39:20,331
Oh, you knew
about that too, Pro Vee?

549
00:39:20,489 --> 00:39:22,990
She's been allergic
since she was little.

550
00:39:23,872 --> 00:39:28,710
Oh, so you and Nana have known
each other since childhood?

551
00:39:32,391 --> 00:39:34,534
I'm such a terrible friend.

552
00:39:34,559 --> 00:39:37,653
I don't pay attention
to anything.

553
00:39:37,955 --> 00:39:39,447
It's okay, Fahsai.

554
00:39:39,472 --> 00:39:41,472
And now I bought this
for nothing.

555
00:39:42,090 --> 00:39:45,587
It's fine. We can give it
to one of the nurses.

556
00:39:45,816 --> 00:39:47,112
That works.

557
00:39:47,793 --> 00:39:51,958
Oh, Nana, did you know
yesterday's fashion show

558
00:39:51,983 --> 00:39:57,441
was all over fashion pages,
sports pages, and society news?

559
00:39:58,123 --> 00:40:01,454
Thanks for helping
as my consultant, Fahsai.

560
00:40:01,874 --> 00:40:05,893
Anytime. Maybe you can repay me

561
00:40:05,918 --> 00:40:09,107
with free golf lessons from Vee.

562
00:40:09,732 --> 00:40:12,765
I've only had
a few lessons with you so far.

563
00:40:12,790 --> 00:40:14,887
Your schedule is packed.

564
00:40:14,912 --> 00:40:17,468
Actually, I was just
about to tell you

565
00:40:17,493 --> 00:40:20,286
that another pro will take over
your remaining lessons.

566
00:40:20,475 --> 00:40:23,040
What? Why?

567
00:40:23,349 --> 00:40:27,312
My schedule got too complicated,
so they've already redone it.

568
00:40:27,337 --> 00:40:29,646
They've assigned you
another pro too,

569
00:40:29,671 --> 00:40:31,696
so your lessons
won't be interrupted.

570
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:34,176
But I want to learn from you.

571
00:40:34,201 --> 00:40:38,003
All the pros are excellent.
They all meet the same standards.

572
00:40:38,062 --> 00:40:39,943
It doesn't matter
which pro you learn from.

573
00:40:39,968 --> 00:40:41,968
It does matter. I...

574
00:40:43,922 --> 00:40:45,161
Excuse me.

575
00:40:51,398 --> 00:40:54,353
The doctor says
you can go home now.

576
00:41:11,629 --> 00:41:13,351
You've taken
your before-meal meds.

577
00:41:13,375 --> 00:41:15,933
Now eat, then take
the after-meal ones.

578
00:41:16,324 --> 00:41:20,509
I had Chef Queen make you
tofu soup with minced pork.

579
00:41:20,534 --> 00:41:22,806
When I was little
and recovering from a fever,

580
00:41:22,831 --> 00:41:26,318
so I'd get better faster.

581
00:41:26,810 --> 00:41:28,318
It looks delicious.

582
00:41:29,995 --> 00:41:32,059
Speaking of your mom,

583
00:41:32,084 --> 00:41:35,282
I really want to go back
and finish the pot we made.

584
00:41:36,368 --> 00:41:39,529
Sure. Let's go see Mom
on my next day off.

585
00:41:39,632 --> 00:41:45,003
But my hands still feel so weak
right now. What should I do?

586
00:41:45,028 --> 00:41:50,215
Oh, sounds like someone needs
another night in the hospital.

587
00:41:51,822 --> 00:41:56,928
Vee, I just want you to feed me.
That's all.

588
00:41:57,407 --> 00:41:59,844
Then just say so. Go on.

589
00:42:00,306 --> 00:42:05,936
Pretty Vee...
please feed me. Please?

590
00:42:06,890 --> 00:42:08,767
See? That wasn't so hard.

591
00:42:09,236 --> 00:42:13,229
Remember, if you want something
from me, just say it straight.

592
00:42:41,278 --> 00:42:42,549
It's so good.

593
00:43:15,843 --> 00:43:19,689
With all our recent projects,
including the fashion show,

594
00:43:19,714 --> 00:43:22,726
we've created a lot of buzz
around the course.

595
00:43:23,337 --> 00:43:28,613
We've also brought in more
non-golfers visit a golf course.

596
00:43:29,001 --> 00:43:32,351
So I think
we need to build on that

597
00:43:32,376 --> 00:43:34,280
and keep Goodview
in people's minds.

598
00:43:34,348 --> 00:43:37,738
From now on, we'll each create
fun content for the course

599
00:43:37,763 --> 00:43:39,703
based on our strengths.

600
00:43:39,727 --> 00:43:42,347
And every month,
I'll give bonuses

601
00:43:42,372 --> 00:43:45,284
to the top five people
with the most views.

602
00:43:45,368 --> 00:43:49,212
I love it.
But I have no idea what to make.

603
00:43:49,795 --> 00:43:53,898
Food, obviously.
Make food content.

604
00:43:56,356 --> 00:43:59,423
Everyone!

605
00:43:59,448 --> 00:44:02,291
I'm sure a lot of you
have already fallen in love

606
00:44:02,316 --> 00:44:04,783
with my cooking at Goodview.

607
00:44:05,113 --> 00:44:07,892
Birdie Bites!

608
00:44:07,917 --> 00:44:11,054
Today, I'm teaching you
something super easy.

609
00:44:11,079 --> 00:44:13,307
If you can make it, make it.
If you can eat it, eat it.

610
00:44:13,332 --> 00:44:14,725
If not, throw it away!

611
00:44:14,750 --> 00:44:16,565
Before every round,

612
00:44:16,590 --> 00:44:20,707
you should always warm up first.
Let's start with this stretch.

613
00:44:20,974 --> 00:44:23,695
Rest the golf club across
the back of your shoulders.

614
00:44:23,720 --> 00:44:25,434
Stand with your feet
shoulder-width apart,

615
00:44:25,459 --> 00:44:27,459
then rotate your torso
to the left.

616
00:44:29,430 --> 00:44:31,372
Then rotate to the right.

617
00:44:33,285 --> 00:44:35,158
This helps stretch your spine.

618
00:44:36,019 --> 00:44:38,172
Give it a try at home.

619
00:44:40,872 --> 00:44:43,743
Hi, everyone.
Welcome to Golf by the Green.

620
00:44:43,768 --> 00:44:47,791
Today, I'm taking you to see
the toughest hole on our course.

621
00:44:47,816 --> 00:44:52,487
It's a par-5 island hole,
the longest on the course,

622
00:44:52,512 --> 00:44:54,547
and the windiest, too.

623
00:44:54,968 --> 00:44:56,721
Hi, everyone.
On today's Caddie Secrets,

624
00:44:56,746 --> 00:44:58,584
I'll show you
how to read a green,

625
00:44:58,608 --> 00:45:01,603
the way even some pros
have to ask their caddies about.

626
00:45:01,628 --> 00:45:04,843
I'll show you what to look for
before making your shot.

627
00:45:16,748 --> 00:45:19,501
Your course is really making
a name for itself these days.

628
00:45:19,526 --> 00:45:20,674
Seen the news?

629
00:45:20,769 --> 00:45:24,371
Goodview clips keep popping up
on my phone every day.

630
00:45:25,589 --> 00:45:30,418
Seriously. My wife even knows
all your caddies by name now.

631
00:45:30,434 --> 00:45:32,116
She even makes me
book them for her.

632
00:45:32,141 --> 00:45:35,003
- That's dangerous.
- Tell me about it.

633
00:45:35,028 --> 00:45:36,193
You'd better watch out.

634
00:45:36,218 --> 00:45:38,658
Your daughter's really something.

635
00:45:38,683 --> 00:45:40,436
Didn't you say
she studied fashion?

636
00:45:40,461 --> 00:45:42,000
Yeah, she graduated in fashion.

637
00:45:42,868 --> 00:45:45,672
She takes after her old man
in every way.

638
00:45:45,697 --> 00:45:47,809
- She's just like me.
- That's good.

639
00:45:47,834 --> 00:45:50,820
Once she sets her mind
on something, she never lets go.

640
00:45:50,845 --> 00:45:54,023
Then I guess you don't have to
worry anymore.

641
00:45:54,048 --> 00:45:56,549
You thought it was done for,
and now it's bouncing right back.

642
00:45:56,668 --> 00:45:58,804
- Yeah.
- Come on.

643
00:45:58,829 --> 00:46:01,456
Guys our age need to know
when to step aside

644
00:46:01,481 --> 00:46:03,734
and let our kids take over.

645
00:46:05,999 --> 00:46:11,086
Hey, I ran into Wut last week.
He said he's beaten cancer.

646
00:46:11,315 --> 00:46:13,672
Cancer can actually be cured?

647
00:46:13,696 --> 00:46:16,476
Of course.
Doctors are amazing these days.

648
00:46:16,501 --> 00:46:18,255
Speaking of which,

649
00:46:18,280 --> 00:46:21,199
when are you starting that chemo
your doctor recommended?

650
00:46:21,556 --> 00:46:23,316
The longer you wait,
the worse it could get

651
00:46:23,341 --> 00:46:25,341
and become harder to treat.

652
00:46:28,185 --> 00:46:31,362
My doctor wants me to start
treatment right away, too.

653
00:46:33,313 --> 00:46:35,646
I just need a little more time
to come to terms with it.

654
00:46:36,559 --> 00:46:39,638
Hey, no matter
how much money you have...

655
00:46:40,469 --> 00:46:42,072
If something happens to you,

656
00:46:42,097 --> 00:46:44,097
you won't even be around
to spend all that money.

657
00:46:44,654 --> 00:46:47,802
- Is that a warning or a curse?
- Maybe both.

658
00:46:49,772 --> 00:46:54,630
Seriously, though, you should
tell your kids about it.

659
00:46:57,208 --> 00:46:58,217
Yeah.

660
00:47:09,349 --> 00:47:10,389
Hi, Mom.

661
00:47:10,414 --> 00:47:11,842
- Hello, Aunt Sinee.
- Hello, dear.

662
00:47:11,867 --> 00:47:15,344
- You're feeling better now?
- I'm all better.

663
00:47:15,369 --> 00:47:16,895
Thank you for worrying about me.

664
00:47:16,920 --> 00:47:19,135
Want to come see the vase
you made last time?

665
00:47:19,160 --> 00:47:21,918
I've already fired it.
You can paint it today.

666
00:47:22,546 --> 00:47:24,419
- Let's go.
- Okay.

667
00:47:30,250 --> 00:47:34,095
It looks kind of weird. It's not
as pretty as your other pieces.

668
00:47:35,143 --> 00:47:37,347
It matches your personality.

669
00:47:38,291 --> 00:47:39,960
Are you saying I'm weird?

670
00:47:39,985 --> 00:47:45,512
Oh, Vee probably means
you have your own unique style.

671
00:47:46,043 --> 00:47:47,075
Right?

672
00:47:48,289 --> 00:47:50,263
- Yes, Mom.
- Mm-hmm.

673
00:47:51,287 --> 00:47:54,644
I've got the paints ready.
You can start whenever you like.

674
00:47:54,669 --> 00:47:56,583
- Okay.
- Vee, help her out.

675
00:47:56,608 --> 00:47:59,203
- Sure.
- Take your time.

676
00:48:09,030 --> 00:48:11,371
First, put on one or two
base coats.

677
00:48:11,396 --> 00:48:12,863
Then you can add
the actual color.

678
00:48:14,182 --> 00:48:16,659
Like putting on primer
before makeup.

679
00:48:16,684 --> 00:48:20,596
Yeah, pretty much. Like this.

680
00:48:25,745 --> 00:48:27,113
Like this.

681
00:48:30,575 --> 00:48:32,427
- Want to try?
- Sure.

682
00:48:35,686 --> 00:48:39,451
Just brush it on. That's it.

683
00:48:52,835 --> 00:48:54,135
Is it pretty, Vee?

684
00:48:56,901 --> 00:48:57,980
Pretty.

685
00:48:58,583 --> 00:49:01,880
This or me? Which one's prettier?

686
00:49:02,563 --> 00:49:04,563
What do you want me to say?

687
00:49:05,442 --> 00:49:09,231
That your Nana
is the prettiest of all.

688
00:49:11,468 --> 00:49:17,106
My Nana is...
the cringiest of all.

689
00:49:17,361 --> 00:49:20,055
Cringiest? What does that mean?

690
00:49:20,080 --> 00:49:24,406
It means cute. Super cute.

691
00:49:24,876 --> 00:49:30,005
I don't think so. Don't lie.
Tell me what it really means.

692
00:49:30,030 --> 00:49:32,664
It means you're pretty, cute,

693
00:49:32,689 --> 00:49:34,387
and basically perfect
in every way.

694
00:49:35,891 --> 00:49:39,305
I don't buy it.
Tell me what it really means.

695
00:49:39,361 --> 00:49:42,561
- You don't trust me?
- Nope.

696
00:49:43,253 --> 00:49:49,233
Tell me what it means, or
I'm smearing paint all over you.

697
00:49:49,766 --> 00:49:52,394
- Hey!
- Don't you dare.

698
00:49:52,419 --> 00:49:56,986
Tell me. Come on, tell me!

699
00:49:59,988 --> 00:50:03,999
- So that's how you wanna play?
- What? What are you doing?

700
00:50:04,024 --> 00:50:06,357
- No!
- You're getting it now.

701
00:50:06,382 --> 00:50:08,986
Vee! Vee!

702
00:50:09,658 --> 00:50:13,744
No! Just tell me, Vee!

703
00:50:14,845 --> 00:50:16,098
- Vee!
- Stop!

704
00:50:41,799 --> 00:50:44,713
Oops... wrong cue.

705
00:50:47,638 --> 00:50:51,052
I'll just...

706
00:50:51,077 --> 00:50:55,681
leave this right here
on the table.

707
00:50:56,016 --> 00:50:59,701
I'm leaving. Sugary sweet!

708
00:51:07,483 --> 00:51:09,680
So shall we finish
this scene, Vee?

709
00:51:19,519 --> 00:51:21,661
We can end it here too.
It's cute this way.

710
00:51:33,086 --> 00:51:37,185
Your cooking was amazing.
I ate way too much.

711
00:51:38,320 --> 00:51:41,873
Chef Queen needs to come
learn some recipes from you.

712
00:51:41,898 --> 00:51:43,146
Anytime.

713
00:51:47,554 --> 00:51:50,826
It's pouring. I don't think
you should drive home.

714
00:51:53,364 --> 00:51:58,413
Exactly. Looks like I'll just
have to stay the night.

715
00:52:14,792 --> 00:52:17,887
The rain's letting up.
You could probably leave now.

716
00:52:21,083 --> 00:52:25,974
I'm so sleepy, Vee.
My eyes are already closing.

717
00:52:31,315 --> 00:52:32,954
You're so sneaky.

718
00:52:35,319 --> 00:52:39,267
Your mom told me I used to
sleep over here a lot as a kid.

719
00:52:40,255 --> 00:52:41,612
Yeah, you did.

720
00:52:41,637 --> 00:52:44,385
Did you ever sleep over
at my house?

721
00:52:44,410 --> 00:52:46,980
Yeah. Quite a few times.

722
00:52:47,325 --> 00:52:50,232
Really?
I don't remember that at all.

723
00:52:51,070 --> 00:52:54,426
Little Nana used to talk about
getting married all the time.

724
00:52:54,659 --> 00:52:57,779
Married? What did I say?

725
00:53:02,484 --> 00:53:05,090
What are you drawing, Nana?

726
00:53:05,479 --> 00:53:08,949
- Me when I grow up.
- And who's this?

727
00:53:11,004 --> 00:53:14,392
- That's my sweetheart.
- You already have one?

728
00:53:14,868 --> 00:53:16,804
Not yet.
I'll have one when I grow up,

729
00:53:16,829 --> 00:53:18,829
and we'll get married like this.

730
00:53:21,796 --> 00:53:25,958
That's you, Vee. You have to
come to my wedding too.

731
00:53:31,282 --> 00:53:32,477
Really?

732
00:53:32,691 --> 00:53:34,580
Really. And there's more.

733
00:53:34,605 --> 00:53:36,909
What else? Tell me.

734
00:53:39,619 --> 00:53:44,033
You must be tired from golfing.
Let's sit here and rest.

735
00:53:53,051 --> 00:53:54,929
Those flowers are so pretty.

736
00:53:54,954 --> 00:53:57,905
You like them?
I can make you a flower crown.

737
00:53:57,930 --> 00:53:59,519
Then I'll make one too.

738
00:54:22,221 --> 00:54:23,793
This one's for you.

739
00:54:25,880 --> 00:54:27,627
Then this one's for you.

740
00:54:35,114 --> 00:54:37,429
- Thank you.
- So pretty.

741
00:54:38,233 --> 00:54:39,622
Nana.

742
00:54:40,738 --> 00:54:41,904
What?

743
00:54:43,491 --> 00:54:46,300
When we grow up,
let's get married.

744
00:54:46,616 --> 00:54:50,505
Okay. When I grow up,
I'll marry you, Vee.

745
00:54:51,047 --> 00:54:53,563
- Promise?
- Promise.

746
00:55:00,641 --> 00:55:04,637
Oh, I was precocious
even back then.

747
00:55:05,322 --> 00:55:08,944
You've probably forgotten
all about that promise by now.

748
00:55:11,020 --> 00:55:12,886
I did forget.

749
00:55:17,322 --> 00:55:19,737
But I won't forget it again.

750
00:55:29,051 --> 00:55:30,222
What do you mean?

751
00:55:32,547 --> 00:55:36,298
I'll admit, I barely remember
any of what you just told me.

752
00:55:37,178 --> 00:55:39,178
But if I really said that
back then,

753
00:55:39,713 --> 00:55:41,442
then I have to keep my promise.

754
00:55:49,539 --> 00:55:51,695
A promise you made
when you were six?

755
00:55:54,615 --> 00:55:59,402
What if that six-year-old girl
still stands by her promise...

756
00:56:04,821 --> 00:56:07,537
and she's here to claim it now?

757
00:56:13,281 --> 00:56:15,139
What would you say, Vee?

758
00:59:48,586 --> 00:59:51,831
Miss Nana, this is bad.
Something serious has happened.

759
00:59:51,856 --> 00:59:54,759
The dead fish stink
all the way into the houses.

760
00:59:54,784 --> 00:59:56,046
(No to polluted water!)

761
00:59:56,070 --> 00:59:58,347
But the fish floating dead
are saltwater fish,

762
00:59:58,372 --> 00:59:59,744
not freshwater fish.

763
01:00:00,846 --> 01:00:04,564
Are you saying someone's
trying to sabotage our course?

764
01:00:05,199 --> 01:00:07,516
So you think
Pro Vee had something to do

765
01:00:07,541 --> 01:00:09,873
with the smear campaign
against our course?

766
01:00:10,355 --> 01:00:12,410
She's done something
like this before.

767
01:00:12,435 --> 01:00:13,993
Why wouldn't she do it again?

768
01:00:18,907 --> 01:00:23,141
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

769
01:00:24,009 --> 01:00:28,624
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

770
01:00:29,092 --> 01:00:33,564
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

771
01:00:34,276 --> 01:00:38,689
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

772
01:00:39,351 --> 01:00:44,522
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

773
01:00:44,547 --> 01:00:49,295
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

774
01:00:49,320 --> 01:00:52,681
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

775
01:00:52,706 --> 01:00:55,232
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

776
01:00:55,257 --> 01:01:00,735
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

777
01:01:00,760 --> 01:01:03,868
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

778
01:01:03,893 --> 01:01:08,665
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

779
01:01:09,955 --> 01:01:13,100
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

780
01:01:13,125 --> 01:01:15,828
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

781
01:01:15,853 --> 01:01:21,451
♪ Sometimes this tender heart
may despair ♪

782
01:01:21,476 --> 01:01:24,708
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

783
01:01:24,733 --> 01:01:27,148
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

784
01:01:27,173 --> 01:01:30,739
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

785
01:01:32,774 --> 01:01:37,524
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

786
01:01:38,081 --> 01:01:42,673
♪ A thousand rounds,
it'd still choose you ♪

787
01:01:43,151 --> 01:01:47,973
♪ One look in your eyes
is all I need ♪

788
01:01:47,998 --> 01:01:51,500
♪ Oh, baby. I trust your sweet. ♪
